## 🔹 TCP vs UDP Comparison

| Feature            | TCP                           | UDP                          |
| ------------------ | ----------------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| Full Name          | Transmission Control Protocol | User Datagram Protocol       |
| OSI Layer          | Transport Layer               | Transport Layer              |
| Connection         | Connection-oriented           | Connectionless               |
| Reliability        | Reliable                      | Unreliable / best-effort     |
| Acknowledgement    | Yes                           | No                           |
| Retransmission     | Yes                           | No                           |
| Packet ordering    | Yes                           | No                           |
| 3-way handshake    | Yes                           | No                           |
| Flow control       | Yes                           | No                           |
| Congestion control | Yes                           | No                           |
| Error recovery     | Yes                           | Limited                      |
| Header size        | Minimum 20 bytes              | 8 bytes                      |
| Speed              | Generally slower              | Generally faster             |
| Overhead           | Higher                        | Lower                        |
| Latency            | Generally higher              | Generally lower              |
| Broadcast          | No                            | Can be used by applications  |
| Multicast          | No                            | Commonly used                |
| Best for           | Reliable data transfer        | Fast/real-time communication |

